From 33646af430db1ada6a35ae959076bbd4184246c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 13:12:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/23] feat(web): product-first listing card and offer detail
 polish

Rework the marketplace listing card into a product-first layout: landscape
4:3 photo, two-line title, key-spec line built from listing facts and
location, price as the single warm accent, and the store line at the foot.
Drop the pull-box metaphor, hidden lid element, and archive code; the title
button's hit area now stretches across the whole card.

Move ListingSheet out of Overlays into its own module, surface the price
directly under the title, render the facts grid only when it has content,
and show the long description after the facts.

Remap the sheet's legacy local tokens onto the retail theme so the offer
detail follows palettes and dark mode, add a --retail-price token, and match
the loading skeleton to the new landscape cards.
